The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

poiseuille1:

 Viscoelastic multi-mode problem on a unit square.
 Start-up of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow rate. 
 Upper half of the domain using symmetry boundary conditions at the bottom.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance for logc=1, but is recommended to use logc=0 for this
 problem.
 second-order time integration

poiseuille2:

 Elastoviscoplastic problem on a unit square.
 Start-up of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow rate. 
 Upper half of the domain using symmetry boundary conditions at the bottom.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance for logc=1, but is recommended to use logc=0 for this
 problem.
 second-order time integration

 Similar to poiseuille1 with an extension to an evp model.

poiseuille3:

 Elastoviscoplastic problem on a unit square.
 Start-up of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow rate. 
 Upper half of the domain using symmetry boundary conditions at the bottom.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order time integration

 Similar to poiseuille2, but now using the b-formulation.

poiseuille4:

 Elastoviscoplastic problem on a unit square.
 Saramito model (2021) with Drucker-Prager plasticity.
 Start-up of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow rate. 
 Upper half of the domain using symmetry boundary conditions at the bottom.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance for logc=1, but is recommended to use logc=0 for this
 problem.
 second-order time integration

 Similar to poiseuille2, but now using the Saramito DP plasticity model.

poiseuille5:

 Start-up of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow rate.
 Incompressible EGP model using the conformation tensor formulation.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

poiseuille6:

 Sequence of steady states of plane Poiseuille flow having a constant flow
 rate for an incompressible EGP model using the conformation tensor
 formulation. 
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.


